## Notes on the acceptance criteria

| AC | Where |
|---|---|
| 1. Bucket versioned / encrypted / private | `BucketVersioningV2`, `BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2`, `BucketPublicAccessBlock` + `BucketOwnershipControls` + TLS-only bucket policy |
| 2. RDS hardened | `deletionProtection: true`, `backupRetentionPeriod` 7 (dev) / 30 (prod), `publiclyAccessible: false`, `storageEncrypted` + `multiAz` on prod. Resource is `protect: true` so `pulumi destroy` won't nuke it accidentally. |
| 3. Secret never plaintext | `pulumi config set --secret` → encrypted in `Pulumi.<stack>.yaml`; `pulumi.secret()` keeps it encrypted in state; runtime copy lives in Secrets Manager. If no password supplied, `random.RandomPassword` generates one that never leaves state. |
| 4. Least privilege | IRSA policy lists explicit actions scoped to the bucket ARN and the one secret ARN — no `*` actions, no `*` resources. |
| 5. Cluster sizing | `ManagedNodeGroup` driven by `nodeCount`/`nodeInstanceType` stack config. |
| 6. HTTPS | ALB listener on 443 with ACM `certificateArn`, TLS 1.3 policy, no forced 80→443 redirect. |
| 7. Env isolation | Separate stacks (`dev`, `prod`) = separate state files and separate config files. `pulumi up -s prod` cannot touch dev resources. |

**Deploy:**
```bash
pulumi stack select dev  && pulumi up
pulumi stack select prod && pulumi up
```
